  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Evaluation of the UK&apos;s Framework for Results for Malaria in the Developing World and Choices for Women:Planned Pregnancies, Safe Births and Healthy Newborns</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity Monitoring and Evaluation of the UK&apos;s Framework for Results for Malaria in the Developing World and Choices for Women:Planned Pregnancies, Safe Births and Healthy Newborns is a component of Monitoring and Evaluation of the UK&apos;s Framework for Results for Malaria in the Developing World and Choices for Women: Planned Pregnancies, Safe Births and Healthy Newborns. reported by FCDO with a funding type of 104 - Procurement of Services and a budget of &#xA3;651,049. This project benefits Developing countries, unspecified. It works in the following sector(s): Reproductive health care, Basic health care, Family planning, Malaria control.</narrative>
  </description>
